Package: GDAinference
Title: Combinatorial Inference in Geometric Data Analysis
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Abel", "Aussant", email = "abel.aussant@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Exact combinatorial (permutation) inference tests for Geometric
    Data Analysis (GDA). The package implements the multidimensional
    typicality and homogeneity tests introduced by Le Roux, Bienaise and
    Durand (2019, "Combinatorial Inference in Geometric Data Analysis",
    Chapman & Hall/CRC). Tests operate on the principal coordinates produced
    by common GDA methods and integrate natively with the 'FactoMineR',
    'GDAtools' and 'ade4' packages, as well as with plain coordinate matrices.
    Each test returns a p-value from the combinatorial distribution of a
    Mahalanobis-type statistic, together with a compatibility region. Unlike
    the chi-squared approximations sometimes used in practice, the tests are
    exact (exhaustive enumeration when feasible, Monte Carlo otherwise).
